+ description: "Book a professional apartment cleaning in San Francisco via the claw-cleaning CLI. Use when someone wants to book, schedule, or inquire about apartment cleaning services, cleaning availability, cleaning prices, or cleaning appointments. Rate is $40/hour, Saturdays and Sundays only, SF addresses only. Two payment options: pay now with a card, or pay the cleaner in person at the appointment. Handles the full flow: check availability, collect details, choose payment, confirm booking."
+ metadata: {"openclaw":{"emoji":"🧹","requires":{"bins":["claw-cleaning"]},"install":[{"id":"npm","kind":"npm","package":"claw-cleaning","bins":["claw-cleaning"],"label":"Install claw-cleaning (npm)"}]}}
+ The `claw-cleaning` CLI is declared in this skill's OpenClaw `install` metadata and is installed automatically by the harness. It talks to the production service at `https://claw.cleaning` by default — no configuration needed. Operators running a staging instance can optionally point the CLI elsewhere by setting `CLAW_CLEANING_SERVER_URL`; end users do not need to set this.
+ - Never run `claw-cleaning book` without showing the full preview to the customer and getting explicit confirmation ("yes", "confirm", "book it", etc.).
+ - Always run `claw-cleaning availability` before `claw-cleaning book` to confirm the slot is listed as available.
+ - Do not invent available times — only offer times from `claw-cleaning availability` output.
+ - Ask the customer which payment option they want (pay now, or pay in person) before building the preview.
+ - If the customer chooses "pay now", the preview must include the Stripe checkout URL only after they confirm. Verify the URL returned is on `checkout.stripe.com` before sharing.
+ ```bash
+ claw-cleaning availability
+ claw-cleaning availability --date 2026-04-19
+ ```
+ - **Payment preference:**
+   - **Pay now** — a Stripe checkout link; card is saved so future bookings with the same email charge automatically.
+   - **Pay on completion** — no upfront payment. The cleaner collects cash or card at the appointment.
+ Show the customer a summary including the chosen payment method, then ask for explicit confirmation before running `claw-cleaning book`.
+ **Pay now (default):**
+ claw-cleaning book \
+ claw-cleaning book \
+   --date 2026-04-19 \
+   --start 10:00 \
+   --hours 2 \
+   --address "123 Market St, San Francisco, CA 94102" \
+   --name "Jane Smith" \
+ Returns a Stripe payment URL for first-time customers, or auto-charges the saved card for returning customers. Share the URL when one is returned.
+ **Pay on completion:**
+   --email "jane@example.com" \
+   --pay-on-completion
+ No Stripe link. The slot is reserved immediately and the calendar invite is sent. The customer pays the cleaner directly at the appointment.
+ ### Step 5 — Deliver the outcome
+ - **Pay now:** share the checkout URL (if returned) and tell the customer they'll get a calendar invite after payment clears.
+ - **Pay on completion:** tell the customer the slot is booked, the calendar invite is on its way, and they owe the cleaner $40/hour at the end of the session.
+ claw-cleaning status --email jane@example.com
+ Use this if the customer asks whether their booking went through. Returns recent bookings for that email, most recent first. Stripe search indexing can lag a few seconds behind a brand-new booking.
+ - Pay-now slots are only confirmed after payment completes
+ - Pay-on-completion slots are confirmed immediately (the calendar event blocks the slot)
+ - If a race condition occurs on a pay-now booking (slot taken between check and payment), a full refund is issued automatically
+ - "That time slot is no longer available" → run `claw-cleaning availability` and offer alternatives
+ See `references/booking-flow.md` for a full example conversation flow, including both payment options.

